# --- Go build artifacts ---
# Default binary name (when running `go build` without -o).
/bishop-memory
# Per-command build binaries (from `go build ./cmd/memoryd` etc. in module root).
/memoryd
/mcpd
# Everything the Makefile's `build` and `dist-linux*` targets produce
# (bin/memoryd, bin/memoryd-linux-amd64, bin/memoryd-linux-arm64, and
# any future platform/arch this project adds a dist-* target for) —
# one blanket rule on the directory rather than naming each binary, so
# a new cross-compile target never needs a matching .gitignore edit.
/bin/
# Cross-compiled Windows binaries.
*.exe
# `go test -c` compiled test binaries. Not produced by `make test`/CI
# (which run plain `go test`, never `-c`), but a common enough local
# debugging step that it is worth covering pre-emptively.
*.test
# `go test -coverprofile=...`/`go tool pprof` output, if run locally.
# Not produced by the Makefile or CI today, but a likely first thing a
# contributor reaches for, and the whole point of this pass is that a
# stray artefact like this must never reach a commit by accident.
coverage.out
*.prof

# --- Local data: SQLite database files ---
# The DB lives under data/ and uses WAL mode, which produces -wal / -shm
# sibling files alongside the main database. Both naming conventions are
# covered (Makefile uses *.db; README documents *.sqlite as a future
# option).
data/*.sqlite
data/*.db
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm
data/*.sqlite-wal
data/*.sqlite-shm

# --- Local environment files ---
# .env holds secrets (PORT, DB_PATH, LOG_LEVEL, future API keys).
# .env.example is checked in.
.env

# --- Vendored dependencies (unused; kept for cleanliness if anyone runs `go mod vendor`) ---
/vendor/

# --- Note: cmd/memoryd/main_test.go's subprocess test -----------------
# TestGracefulShutdown_OnSIGTERM builds a throwaway memoryd binary and a
# throwaway SQLite database, but both live under t.TempDir() (an
# OS-managed temp directory outside this repo, removed automatically
# when the test finishes) — nothing it writes ever lands inside this
# tree, so no dedicated ignore rule is needed for it.
#
# WARNING: this test does NOT exercise `go build ./cmd/...` in the module
# root. Manual `go build ./cmd/memoryd` and `go build ./cmd/mcpd` writes
# binaries to the module root, which are now covered by the explicit
# /memoryd and /mcpd rules above. A full build-all-commands verification
# must clean those binaries after building.

# --- Editor / OS scratch ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
